  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday Night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1116 AM CDT Fri Jun 26 2026\n\nLow to medium rain and storm chances will continue Sunday across the \neast. But the main story from here into next week will be the heat. \nStrong high pressure will start to build across the southeast US \nSunday and will be the dominant feature across the eastern CONUS \nthrough the upcoming week. This will keep us mainly dry, but allow \ntemperatures to warm with highs reaching the mid and upper-90s and\novernight temperatures only dropping into the mid and upper-70s. \nHeat index values will be even warmer with triple digits expected \neach afternoon. Several days of this prolonged heat will be \nimpactful as heat risk will be major to extreme Monday into the \nend of the week. \n\nCheck in on one another during this dangerous heat, particularly \nthose more vulnerable to the heat including children, the elderly, \nthose who are pregnant or have a chronic illness, and those who do \nnot have AC.",
